          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "trīticum is built on trītus, the participle of terō 'to rub, to thresh' (EtymDB; Lewis & Short, after an ancient explanation): the grain that is threshed."
            }
          ]
        },
